## CLI flags

./fql select... -> normal query for the cli (by default the query is provided like this but if no query is provided then the cli accepts query from stdin like sqlite3 cli)
./fql --timeout=2s -> each query can only run for 2 seconds
./fql --output=json|text|default:table -> output type
./fql --stats -> metrics related to query e.g. time taken to run, status (failed | success),
./fql --server -> server mode where it accepts queries as requests and returns responses.

## SELECT operations

1) select * from ~ -> select all files & directories from homedir
2) select recursive * from ~ -> select all files & directories recursively from homedir
3) select * from ~ where type = f -> select all files from homedir
4) select * from / where type = d -> select all directories from root dir
5) select * from /usr/bin where type = s,f -> select files that are symlinks in the /usr/bin directory
6) select * from /usr/bin where created_at > 10s -> select files that have existed for more than 10s in the /usr/bin directory
7) select name from Downloads -> select the name of all files & directories in "Downloads" directory

### keypoints
1) in fifth query name is the property of the file. all the other options are "name,size,modified_at,created_at,type"

